# ===== verdict =====
# Gate 0b FAILS on the same condition as Gate 0: no aie_trace* file. The metadata now loads ("AIE metadata read
# successfully from disk!"). The plugin then stops with XDP's AIE_TRACE_UNAVAILABLE: "Neither PLIO nor GMIO trace
# infrastructure is found in the given design". In XDP (profile/plugin/aie_trace/aie_trace_plugin.cpp) that is
# getNumStreamsPLIO() == 0 && getNumStreamsGMIO() == 0, i.e. the design declares no trace streams.
# The metadata agrees: TraceGMIOs is empty. The 16 GMIOs are data (IFM/WGT/OFM), and the 4 PLIOs are TCT0..3,
# not trace. Outputs stayed bit-equal and the xmodel did not recompile.
# Reading: the shipped Phoenix overlay was compiled without trace routing, so XRT's trace plugin cannot observe
# its cores by configuration alone. Declaring trace streams in an edited metadata file was NOT tried: XDP would
# then program routes into the live partition, which is no longer configuration-only observation.
